The given equation is $8 x^2-26 x+15=0$.
$\therefore$ The sum of roots, $\tan \frac{\alpha}{2}+\tan \frac{\beta}{2}=\frac{26}{8}=\frac{13}{4}$ and product of roots, $\tan \frac{\alpha}{2} \cdot \tan \frac{\beta}{2}=\frac{15}{8}\begin{aligned}
& \begin{aligned}
\therefore \tan \left(\frac{\alpha+\beta}{2}\right) & =\frac{\tan \frac{\alpha}{2}+\tan \frac{\beta}{2}}{1-\tan \frac{\alpha}{2} \cdot \tan \frac{\beta}{2}} \\
& =\frac{\frac{13}{4}}{1-\frac{15}{8}}=-\frac{26}{7}
\end{aligned} \\
& \text { Now, } \begin{aligned}
\cos (\alpha+\beta) & =\frac{1-\tan ^2\left(\frac{\alpha+\beta}{2}\right)}{1+\tan ^2\left(\frac{\alpha+\beta}{2}\right)} \\
& =\frac{1-\left(-\frac{26}{7}\right)^2}{1+\left(-\frac{26}{7}\right)^2}=\frac{49-676}{49+676}=-\frac{627}{725}
\end{aligned}
\end{aligned}$
